{
  "about": "The crew's parts (each skinned to a Mathwood people's skeleton, 'm' the men's or 'f' the women's, and carrying it; made by ~/pw/space-math/rigs/crew-rig/) and the characters put together from them (kit/crew.js makeCrew). A recipe: { suit, head, hair, colours: { job, uniform, skin, hair, eyes }, expression, face }; a colour left out keeps the part's own (job: the suit's marks, lines and panels, unless the suit keeps its own colours; uniform: its whites); expression is a visor's face (neutral, happy, thinking, surprised); eyes tints a head's real eyes, face sets its face bones ({ slider: -1..1 }, kit/crew.js FACE) (the Tripo heads, made by ~/pw/space-math/rigs/crew-heads/: eyes and face true). The suit's skeleton sets the clips. Any head goes on any suit and any hair on any head: a head attaches at the Neck and Head joints and hair at the Head joint (the attachment rules: ~/pw/space-math/characters/CHARACTERS.md).",
  "aboutHands": "HANDS (2026-11-07, ~/pw/space-math/rigs/crew-rig/hands.py): a suit is clothing only, open at its cuffs; the hands are their own part (parts.hand: both hands in one mesh, a skin mask so the skin tone tints them, the head's own skin when none is given). A suit wears its skeleton's hands; a recipe's hand names others (an id, or null for none); a suit made with hands of its own says ownHands and wears none unless named.",
  "hairAtlas": { "map": "hair_atlas.webp", "normal": "hair_atlas_n.webp" },
